# Commit cycle — MessengerMapper

Source of truth: `../THE-NEXUS/06-WORKFLOWS/commit-cycle.md`. Trigger intercept: `00-always.mdc`.
Vault authority: `../MessengerMapper-VAULT/` only. Never write lifecycle files to tenant vaults.

## Mandatory cascade
No git sync until STEP 2 passes. STEP 1 runs immediately after COMPILE.

### 0. COMPILE (AI pre-step)
Scan local diff and history. Draft compact narrative. Segment message (right of pipe) must be $\le$ 450 characters. Validate length.
Write narrative directly under `## 2. THE TECHNICAL NARRATIVE` in `HANDOFF.md` before STEP 1.

### STEP 1 — Context compaction
```text
python ../THE-NEXUS/scripts/handoff.py --project-root . --vault-root ../MessengerMapper-VAULT -write MessengerMapper-teardown -success "Category | <summary>"
```
- Exit code must be `0`.
- On rollback/error: replace with `-failure "Category | <description>"` and halt.

### STEP 2 — Vault schema validation
```text
python ../THE-NEXUS/scripts/review-commit.py --project-root . --vault-root ../MessengerMapper-VAULT --sha HEAD --scope reviewer --dry-run
```
- Exit code must be `0`.

### STEP 3 — Git sync (`FULL_LIFECYCLE` only)
Run only when STEP 1 & 2 exit `0`:
1. Stage: `git add .`
2. Commit message: read `HANDOFF.md` Section 2. If empty, use COMPILE narrative segment.
3. Commit: `git commit -m "<payload>"`
4. Push: `git push`

## Error gate
- STEP 1 fail: emit `[FAIL] handoff.py: <stderr>` and halt. Git aborted.
- STEP 2 fail: emit `[FAIL] review-commit.py: <stderr>` and halt. Git aborted.
For `TEARDOWN`: stop after STEP 2 (no git).

## Review trailers (opt-in)
Add to commit footer:
- `Review: yes` -> `reviewer` runs on diff; writes `14-AUDITS/`
- `Review: security` -> `security-auditor` runs on diff; writes `06-SECURITY-REVIEWS/`
- `Review: full` -> both run in parallel

## Forbidden
- Advancing git sync before STEP 1 and 2 succeed.
- Manual vault compaction bypasses.
- `git commit --no-verify` or `git push --force`.
- Committing secrets or PII.
- Routing master state to tenant vaults.
